{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfijDwvzGh69bTh91c8Qp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate for this slot, a refinement of the incumbent, as `chance_face_bias_motif_suspicion`, and the self-check passed. It only ran a short single-chain smoke fit, though, so convergence and novelty are still untested until the full admission fit.\n\n**The change:** the incumbent `person_specific_motif_suspicion` stays exactly as it was, except that people's model of a fair coin no longer treats heads and tails the same. They believe the coin lands on one face slightly more often. That belief is one shared fitted parameter, `logit_theta` (prior Normal(0, 0.5)). It adds `(heads_a − heads_b) · logit_theta` to the chance evidence. That term is scaled by each person's own sensitivity and by the same per-flip length weighting as the rest of the evidence. So among otherwise similar sequences, the one leaning towards the favoured face looks more random.\n\n**Why this change:** of the critique's significant findings, the strongest one that can be modelled is `heads_count_preference`, and it survives the FDR correction. People choose the head-heavier sequence 47.3% of the time, against 48.8% predicted by the incumbent, which treats heads and tails the same. I didn't pick the side-bias finding because `person_side_habit_switch_belief` already covers it. I didn't pick the response-perseveration finding because it depends on trial order, and binding `trial_index` gets a candidate rejected.\n\n**Check results:**\n- **Result:** `OK`, with a smoke-fit ELPD-LOO of −2103.8. The incumbent's full fit scored −2105.7, but the two numbers come from different kinds of fit, so they don't support saying it beats the incumbent.\n- **Convergence:** R-hat couldn't be computed, because a single-chain fit doesn't report one.\n- **PSIS-LOO reliability:** flagged as unreliable on the smoke fit — 8.5% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. I assumed the short fit causes this and didn't check it against the incumbent or change anything. If it's still there in the full fit, the model's comparison scores can't be trusted.\n- **Novelty risk:** the effect in the data is small, so the extra term may only move predictions a little. Admission could reject the model as too similar to the incumbent.\n\nAll three files are in `iter_2/candidate_4/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":76611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1031,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed541231-6203-42a9-830b-b14ea61b9012","uuid":"af334228-e043-4741-8249-24e12e44a871","timestamp":"2026-10-05T07:53:42.978Z","request_id":"req_011CfijDvqFn5XqkArdQPAD6"}
